/-!
# Set (d), master `I₁₃`: the primitive of `p₄`, first parts

The primitive of `p₄` is `F₄(t) = Ψ₄(ξ(t))` (`QED.ThreeLoopD.hasDerivAt_i13F4`), where `Ψ₄`
(`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4`) is a combination of 111 harmonic polylogarithms `H(w; ξ)` of weight at
most five with coefficients in `ℚ[π², ζ(3)][ξ, 1/ξ]` (poles at most `ξ⁻²`). It is assembled from
the parts `ξ ^ j Nⱼ / ξ²` and a constant-coefficient part. This file defines `N₀, N₁, N₂`
(`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4N0`, …) with their derivatives; the coefficients were generated by a
script.

## Main results

* `QED.ThreeLoopD.hasDerivAt_i13Psi4N0`, `QED.ThreeLoopD.hasDerivAt_i13Psi4N1`,
  `QED.ThreeLoopD.hasDerivAt_i13Psi4N2`.
-/

@[expose] public section

